{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["And if it be on the bed, etc. — one who lies or sits on her place of lying, even though he does not touch it — if he touches it he becomes impure until evening. That is to say, or even if he touches the object of lying he becomes impure until evening and does not become impure to defile garments. For the object of lying distinguishes the law of its touching from the law of its carrying: one who carries it defiles a person to defile his garments, but one who touches it defiles only the person, without his garments." "And whatsoever she sits upon — the Sages explained: upon an object of lying."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "I read מרכב as referring to the same category as משכב — a surface/object of lying; the technical contrast is between נוגע (touching) and נושא (carrying)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:48:53.287236583Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}